Hi all,

I am setting up to run analysis on Affymetrix SNP6, 250K Nsp and 250K Sty chip types.
As I read through the current documentation, I've noticed the following items that
may need attention, or I might need clarification:

On page

   http://aroma-project.org/chipTypes/GenomeWideSNP_6

the hyperlinks at

   GenomeWideSNP_6,Full,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ufl (GenomeWideSNP_6,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ufl) - Unit Fragment-Length (UFL) annotation file

GenomeWideSNP_6,Full,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ufl  and (GenomeWideSNP_6,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ufl) yield different file downloads,
(namely GenomeWideSNP_6,Full,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ufl.gz and GenomeWideSNP_6,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ufl.gz respectively)
whereas the hyperlinks at

   GenomeWideSNP_6,Full,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ugp (GenomeWideSNP_6,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ugp) - Unit Genome Position (UGP) annotation file

GenomeWideSNP_6,Full,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ugp and (GenomeWideSNP_6,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ugp) both offer the same file

GenomeWideSNP_6,Full,na31,hg19,HB20110328.ugp.gz

Also, I can not find where to access and download the files

   GenomeWideSNP_6.Full.CDF and GenomeWideSNP_6.CDF

>From what URL are these files available?

(I have a copy of GenomeWideSNP_6.Full.cdf, of size 493291745 bytes dated Apr 13  2007  - is this still valid
or is there a newer version around?)

Best

Steve

