Data from multiple sources is available that would in principle allow
me to do a tumour/normal copy number analysis.  The normal data was
obtained from samples processed using Affymetrix GenomeWideSNP_6
chips whereas the tumour data was obtained from samples processed
using Affymetrix 500K Nsp+Sty chipsets.

Is it possible to do a paired tumour/normal analysis for copy number
changes in aroma.affymetrix given data from these different chip types?

Given the evolution of the development of these chip types, I'm guessing
that many of the 500K probesets are on the SNP6 chip.  Before I spend
hours tracking this down I wanted to check with this group and see
if anyone has already done so, and whether machinery is already in place
within aroma.affymetrix to match probesets across chip types and run
analysis appropriately.

