Yes, merging 500K and GWS6 data is certainly possible;  From Section
'2.1 Overview of the GWS arrays' of the CRMA v2 paper (Bengtsson et
al. 2009; http://aroma-project.org/publications/):

"The GWS6 chip type interrogates 931 946 SNPs and 945 826 CN loci
totaling 1 877 772 loci, whereas GWS5 interrogates 500 568 SNPs and
417 269 CN loci totaling 917 837 unique loci. GWS5 has the same set of
SNPs as the 500K chip set, whereas for GWS6 6238 of those have been
replaced by a newset of 437 616 SNPs."

/Henrik

